## Installation

```bash
# Install the react component
pnpm dlx clinkclang@latest add agent-progress

# Install the svelte component
pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@next add avatar
pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@next add card
pnpm dlx shadcn-svelte@next add progress
pnpm dlx clinkclang@latest add agent-progress-svelte
```

## API Reference
### Customize your agent
`agentName`, `description`, `imgLink` all modify your agent's looks on the component.
```js
<AgentProgress
	agentName="BrainThrust Agent"
	description="Running all your workflows!"
	imgLink="brainthrust.png"
/>
```
### No time to write logic? No problem!
Use the augmented version of the component with built-in event handlers.
Just pass in your event handlers!
```js
// define handleStart, handleStop, etc...
<AgentProgressAug
	// other props here...

	onStart={handleStart}
	onStop={handleStop}
	onResume={handleResume}
	updateProgress={handleProgress}
	pollRateMs={500}
/>
```
The above **augmented** component comes with built-in logic that runs your event handlers for you, complete with state management.

### Your component, your rules
The default `AgentProgress` component is completely modifiable, relying only on shadcn components. The following props are included by default:
<table>
<thead>
  <tr>
    {#each Object.keys(defaultTable[0]) as columnHeading}
      <th>{columnHeading}</th>
    {/each}
  <tr/>
</thead>
<tbody>
  {#each Object.values(defaultTable) as row}
    <tr>
      {#each Object.values(row) as cell}
        <td>{cell}</td>
      {/each}
    </tr>
  {/each}
</tbody>
</table>

The following are included in the **augmented** version of the component:

<table>
<thead>
  <tr>
    {#each Object.keys(augmentedTable[0]) as columnHeading}
      <th>{columnHeading}</th>
    {/each}
  <tr/>
</thead>
<tbody>
  {#each Object.values(augmentedTable) as row}
    <tr>
      {#each Object.values(row) as cell}
        <td>{cell}</td>
      {/each}
    </tr>
  {/each}
</tbody>
</table>